<title>FRANCE: Juppe seeks EU VAT cut on CD-ROMS,on-line services.</title>
<headline>Juppe seeks EU VAT cut on CD-ROMS,on-line services.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Alain Juppe said on Thursday France would call on its European Union partners in June to lower value-added tax (VAT) on CD-ROMS and educational on-line services to 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We've decided to call on our European partners to revise the VAT product categories in June so that the reduction would take effect in the summer, or by September at the latest,&quot; he told a news conference after a government seminar.</p>
<p>President Jacques Chirac had called on the government last Monday to consider such a cut in VAT on CD-ROMS and on-line services.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
